Package: gnome-shell-extension-zark
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         gnome-shell (>= 50)
Enhances: zark
Description: GNOME Shell extension showing the state of zark backups
 Shows the state of zark backups in the top bar: the last backup to each
 drive, a running backup's progress, when zark waits for an answer in its
 terminal, and how full the system pools are. A details dialog lists each
 pool's datasets and each backup drive's points by month, for deciding a
 prune. It notifies an overdue backup, a backup drive plugged in, a
 question waiting in the terminal and a run that stopped answering.
 .
 It is read-only: it reads the status files zark 2.1 or later writes and
 never starts, stops or changes anything. It uses no network.
